        "description": "Given `countries = ['Estonia', 'Finland', 'Sweden', 'Denmark', 'Norway', 'Iceland']` and `numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`:\n1. Use `map` to uppercase all country names: `uppercase_countries` (convert map object to list).\n2. Use `filter` to filter out countries containing 'land': `land_countries` (convert to list).\n3. Use `map` and a `lambda` to square each number in `numbers`: `squared_numbers`.",
        "starterCode": "countries = ['Estonia', 'Finland', 'Sweden', 'Denmark', 'Norway', 'Iceland']\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n\n# Compute uppercase_countries, land_countries, squared_numbers\n",
